sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User (Browser)
    participant API as Backend API
    participant S3Raw as S3 Raw Bucket
    participant SQS as Amazon SQS
    participant Lambda as Lambda Submitter
    participant Batch as AWS Batch (Fargate)
    participant S3Proc as S3 Processed Bucket
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas

    User->>API: POST /api/videos/initiate-upload
    API->>DB: Create record (status = UPLOADING)
    API-->>User: Return pre-signed URL (TTL 15 min)
    User->>S3Raw: PUT source video directly

    User->>API: PATCH /:id/confirm-upload
    API->>DB: Set status = PROCESSING

    S3Raw-->>SQS: Event notification (s3:ObjectCreated)
    SQS-->>Lambda: Event source mapping triggers
    Lambda->>Batch: SubmitJob (VIDEO_ID, RAW_S3_KEY)
    Lambda-->>SQS: Handler returns, message deleted
    Note over Lambda,SQS: Message is deleted when the job is SUBMITTED,<br/>not when transcoding completes

    activate Batch
    Batch->>S3Raw: Download source into container
    Batch->>Batch: FFmpeg transcode 360p / 720p / 1080p
    Batch->>Batch: Emit master.m3u8 + thumbnail.jpg
    Batch->>S3Proc: Upload all .ts segments and manifests
    Batch->>DB: Conditional write status = READY
    deactivate Batch

    Note over Batch,DB: The conditional write (only if not already READY)<br/>is what guards against duplicate jobs, since the<br/>container holds no SQS message to extend
    Note over Batch: Container terminates, Fargate scales to zero
